35. What is a fluent wait in Selenium?

• Fluent wait is a type of explicit wait that defines the maximum amount of time to wait 
  for a condition and the frequency to check the condition before throwing an exception.

36. How do you implement fluent wait in Selenium?

from selenium.webdriver.support.ui import WebDriverWait
from selenium.webdriver.support import expected_conditions as EC

wait = WebDriverWait(driver, 30, poll_frequency=5, ignored_exceptions=[ElementNotVisibleException, ElementNotSelectableException])
element = wait.until(EC.element_to_be_clickable((By.ID, 'element_id')))

