 but the entire value is not known.

9.How do you write an XPath to select the nth child of a parent element?

•To write an XPath expression that selects the nth child of a parent element, you can use the
 position() function or an index in square brackets []. These methods allow you to specify the
 exact position of the child element you want to select.

Syntax:
---------
//parent/child[n]

Examples
--------------
1.Select the 3rd <li> element under any <ul> parent:

//ul/li[3]

This XPath expression selects the third <li> element that is a child of any <ul> element.

2.Select the 2nd <div> child of a specific <div> with an id of "container":

//div[@id='container']/div[2]

This XPath expression selects the second <div> child of a <div> element with an id attribute
 of "container".


